      "seed": 319760175,
      "version": 415,
      "versionNonce": 656710991,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782751180829,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* Feature drift happens when the input data going into a model changes \nover time compared with the data the model was trained on or compared with a known healthy baseline.\n* Production feature events --> Hourly aggregation --> Compute feature statistic --> compare against baseline --> assign health status --> show in model foundry\n\nA model learns patterns from historical feature distributions. If those feature distributions change in production,\n the model may still run successfully, but its predictions can become less reliable.\n-- Availability drift\n-- Null-rate drift\n-- Distribution drift (numerical features)\n-- Categorical drift\n-- Cardinality drift ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Feature drift happens when the input data going into a model changes \nover time compared with the data the model was trained on or compared with a known healthy baseline.\n* Production feature events --> Hourly aggregation --> Compute feature statistic --> compare against baseline --> assign health status --> show in model foundry\n\nA model learns patterns from historical feature distributions. If those feature distributions change in production,\n the model may still run successfully, but its predictions can become less reliable.\n-- Availability drift\n-- Null-rate drift\n-- Distribution drift (numerical features)\n-- Categorical drift\n-- Cardinality drift ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
